# DRY and file size

Keep modules focused. Prefer shared abstractions over copy-paste.

## God files

- **Hard limit:** no source file over **1500 lines** in this project.
- **Soft target:** route files and page components should stay under **500 lines** when practical.
- If a file is growing large, split by responsibility (e.g. `lib/*-db.ts`, `views/*`, `routes/*`) before adding more logic.

## Reduce duplication

Before copying markup or helpers into a second file:

1. **Check existing shared code** — `Layout`, `PageHeader`, `ContentPage`, `StatusPage`, `EventCard`, `ArchiveCard`, `AdminCrudSections`, `AdminEditActions`, `lib/format.ts`, `lib/datetime.ts`.
2. **Extract when repeated twice** — date formatting, thanks/error pages, admin save/delete actions, archive/event cards.
3. **Keep page-specific content in pages** — only extract structure that is truly identical or parameterized.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — duplicate formatter in a page file
function formatDate(iso: string) {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })
}

// ✅ GOOD — import from lib/format.ts
import { formatArchiveDate } from '../lib/format'
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — copy-pasted thanks page shell
<Layout ...><PageHeader .../><section>...</section></Layout>

// ✅ GOOD
<StatusPage {...site} title="..." heading="..." lead="..." ctaHref="/" ctaLabel="Go home" />
```

## New work checklist

- [ ] No new file approaching 1500 lines
- [ ] No duplicated date/time helpers (use `lib/format.ts` / `lib/datetime.ts`)
- [ ] No duplicated admin save/delete form pairs (use `AdminEditActions`)
- [ ] No duplicated status/thanks page layout (use `StatusPage`)
- [ ] Remove dead/orphan page files when routes move to CMS or shared components
